<%@ Control Language="vb" AutoEventWireup="false" CodeBehind="HowToPlay.ascx.vb" Inherits="Predictathon.UserControls.Rules.HowToPlay" %>
<div class="InformationBlock NoHover">
    <div class="TitleBar">How to play</div>
    <div style="margin: 6px">
        How to play 


        --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        Click the FIXTURES link to view the match calendar. You can see which future days contain matches, and which you have yet to predict. You can add score predictions for each game, or change existing predictions. You can change your mind as many times as you like up to 30 minutes before each kick-off. At kick-off everyone's predictions can be viewed so you can check we're not cheating. Your points will be automatically calculated after each match day and the league table updated. 

        If you know you'll be away from your computer for a few days, make sure you get all your predictions done early. People so often miss out on vital points due to bad planning and forgetfulness. We recommend you predict at least a week ahead; don't rely on remembering to update on Friday afternoons. You'll get a reminder e-mail from us on Friday mornings if you have unpredicted matches in the week ahead. The only way to avoid these potentially annoying e-mails is to make sure you predict well in advance: you can always change your predictions nearer to kick-off. 

        We're not doing anything for weeks with no Premier League matches (e.g. FA Cup weeks and Internationals), we don't want to complicate things with other random stuff. Plus it will be harder work to adapt the website. We're lazy. 

        Click on another person's name on the league page and you can read their profile. This gives you their idiotic personal profile along with stats/trophies and past predictions. Know your enemy. 

        If you want to share your thoughts on football issues, music, politics, kittens, life in general, or just to send abuse to your rubbish opponents, use the sexy message board. You can post youtube videos and pictures should you get the urge. There's all sorts of interesting shit you can post, don't just use it for bullying. Unless it's funny bullying of course. Please use the wonderful “NSFW” function if you’re posting an image and your name is Wonker or Moog, or even if you’re not them and you have something sordid to post. 

        The ever-popular blog function is still around for those among you who have lots to say. You can use it for regular commentary on any subject that floats your boat, a serialised peice of fiction, your life story year by year, or just for one-off messages that you want the predicting world to see. Any boring bloggers will be put in their place on the message board no doubt. 

        Prizes 


        --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

        The full prize list will be announced once the season kicks off. There will be small monthly prizes for the best short-term predictors and bigger cash given to those heroes who finish the season in the top few league positions. Just because you're bottom of the league now doesn't mean you can't win some cash in the monthly leagues, so stick with it losers - people who give up early in this game are twats who won't be invited back for future games. 

        Other random trophies will be awarded throughout the season, they have no monetary value but will make you look cool, with the exception of the (rarely awarded) Bastard of the Week trophy. Don’t anger me or it’ll be coming your way. 

        All of the entry money goes towards the prize fund; we don't make any profit from this game. This may look like a slick commercial enterprise but it's really just a simple game played between friends. 
    </div>
</div>